<title>UK: UK Nov global trade deficit 959 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Nov global trade deficit 959 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following data on Britain's global trade in November(in million stg, previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    GLOBAL TRADE	     NOV	   OCT	(PREL OCT)</p>
<p>    Trade balance	   -959	  -680	  (-454)</p>
<p>    Exports		    13,877	14,407   (14,621)</p>
<p>    Imports		    14,836	15,087   (15,075)</p>
<p>    EU trade balance	-260	   -227	  (-36)</p>
<p>    EU exports		  7,869	 8,143    (8,373)</p>
<p>    EU imports		  8,129	 8,370    (8,409)</p>
<p>    TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS     NOV	OCT   (PREL OCT)</p>
<p>    Trade balance (in million stg)    -1,664   -1,281  (-1,098)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports) 2.0%    1.5%     (1.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports) 1.5%    2.0%     (2.5%)</p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 130.9   128.7    (128.3)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 141.8   145.3    (146.9)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports) 2.5%    2.0%	(2.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps) 8.5%    7.5%	(7.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports) 2.0%    2.5%	(3.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps) 8.0%    8.5%	(9.0%)</p>
<p>    TRADE IN OIL (VALUE MLN STG)	NOV     OCT   (PREL OCT)</p>
<p>    BALANCE				   510     417	(448)</p>
<p>    EXPORTS				 1,008     953	(987)</p>
<p>    IMPORTS				   498     536	(539)</p>
<p>Economists had forecast a deficit of 770 million stg.</p>
<p>The ONS said the global trend for Britain's trade deficit was narrowing.</p>
<p>November's provisional estimates show export prices fell by one percent and import prices fell by three percent compared with October. In the three months ended November export prices fell by 0.5 percent and import prices dropped one percent.  </p>
<p>For 1996, the ONS said the non-EU trade deficit is provisionally estimated at 9.0 billion stg compared with 7.4 billion in 1995. Export volume was up 8.5 percent from last year while import volumes rose 13 percent.</p>
